From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: nss: pad short frames before handing them to the firmware

When a station associates, mac80211 sends an 802.2 Layer 2 Update
frame so that bridges relearn the station's port
(ieee80211_send_layer2_update): a broadcast destination, the station
as source, an 802.3 length field of six and a six byte LLC XID - 20
bytes in total, with skb->protocol set to ETH_P_802_2.

With wifili offload this is the first data frame the firmware is
handed for a new station, and it is 40 bytes below the minimum
Ethernet frame. The QSDK stack these firmware images are validated
against runs qca-wifi rather than mac80211 and has no equivalent
frame, so the path is untested there.

Pad short frames to ETH_ZLEN before handing them over, which is what
the hardware transmit path does for the same frame in host mode.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -1167,8 +1167,22 @@
 		goto drop;
 	}
 
-	if (encap_type == HAL_TCL_ENCAP_TYPE_ETHERNET)
+	if (encap_type == HAL_TCL_ENCAP_TYPE_ETHERNET) {
+		/* mac80211 emits a 20 byte 802.2 Layer 2 Update frame every
+		 * time a station associates (ieee80211_send_layer2_update):
+		 * broadcast DA, the station as SA, an 802.3 length field and
+		 * a six byte LLC XID. It is well below the 60 byte Ethernet
+		 * minimum, and it is the first data frame the firmware sees
+		 * for a new station. The QSDK stack this firmware ships with
+		 * has no equivalent, so pad the frame to a valid length
+		 * before handing it over.
+		 */
+		if (skb->len < ETH_ZLEN && skb_put_padto(skb, ETH_ZLEN)) {
+			atomic_inc(&soc_stats->tx_err.misc_fail);
+			return NSS_TX_FAILURE;
+		}
 		goto send;
+	}
 
 	if (encap_type == HAL_TCL_ENCAP_TYPE_RAW)
 		ath11k_nss_tx_encap_raw(skb);
